  "convention": "Stratified Newcombe interval for the candidate minus baseline difference of equal-weighted mean pass rates. Per arm, the Yan and Su (2010) stratified Wilson interval: p = (1/K) sum s_k/n_k, n_eff = 1 / sum 1/(K^2 n_k), Wilson score interval at (p, n_eff); the arms are combined with Newcombe's hybrid rule (method 10). statsmodels has no stratified Wilson interval, so these values come from an independent Python implementation in generate.py: p and n_eff as exact fractions, the bounds as the roots of (p - x)^2 n_eff = z^2 x (1 - x) in 60-digit decimal arithmetic, with z = scipy.stats.norm.ppf. Entries with one scenario are also checked against statsmodels confint_proportions_2indep(method='newcomb') to 1e-12. Each arm lists (successes, trials) per scenario, in the same scenario order.",
